   "textLength": 594,
   "text": "I am guessing that the problem you are referring to is the fact that you see ==> -s in the output. That suggests you have a file named -s in the directory you are running the script in, and has nothing to do with your script. Before your script is even run, the shell will expand -?. And since ? in shell globs means \"any single character\", the -? is expanded to -s, the only matching file name.\nTo a",
